## DESCRIPTION
## Compute vectors between points.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## KEYWORDS('vectors', 'points')

## DBsubject('Linear Algebra')
## DBchapter('Vector geometry')
## DBsection('Vectors and vector arithmetic')
## Date('September 5, 2011')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

# updated 2022.12.12

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',        'PGML.pl',
    'parserVectorUtils.pl', 'parserParametricLine.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context('Vector')->variables->add(t => 'Real');

($x1, $y1) = (non_zero_random(-5, 5), non_zero_random(-5, 5));
($x2, $y2) = (non_zero_random(-5, 5), non_zero_random(-5, 5));
$ans1 = Vector($x2 - $x1, $y2 - $y1);

($a1, $b1, $c1) =
    (non_zero_random(-5, 5), non_zero_random(-5, 5), non_zero_random(-5, 5));
($a2, $b2, $c2) =
    (non_zero_random(-5, 5), non_zero_random(-5, 5), non_zero_random(-5, 5));
$ans2 = Vector($a2 - $a1, $b2 - $b1, $c2 - $c1);

$ans3 = ParametricLine("<$a1,$b1,$c1>+t*$ans2");

BEGIN_PGML
For all of the following problems, enter a vector with angle brackets.  For example, [` \langle 1,2\rangle`] or[` \langle 1,2,3\rangle`]


a) Find the vector from [` ([$x1],[$y1]) `] to [` ([$x2],[$y2]) `]:  [____]{$ans1}

b) Find the vector from [` ([$a1],[$b1],[$c1]) `] to [` ([$a2],[$b2],[$c2]) `]:  [____]{$ans2}

c) Write the line from [` ([$a1],[$b1],[$c1]) `] to [` ([$a2],[$b2],[$c2]) `] in the form [`\vec{u} + t \vec{v}`]:  [____]{$ans3}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

a) A vector from a point [`(x_1,y_1)`] to [`(x_2,y_2)`] is found with the vector
	[` \begin{bmatrix} x_2-x_1 \\ y_2-y_1 \end{bmatrix}`]

	In this situation, the vector is

	[``\begin{bmatrix} x_2-x_1 \\ y_2-y_1 \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} [$x2]-[$x1] \\ [$y2]-[$y1] \end{bmatrix}
	= \begin{bmatrix} [@ $x2-$x1 @] \\ [@ $y2-$y1@] \end{bmatrix} ``]

a) A vector from a point [`(x_1,y_1,z_1)`] to [`(x_2,y_2,z_2)`] is found with the vector
	[` \begin{bmatrix} x_2-x_1 \\ y_2-y_1 \\ z_2-z_1 \end{bmatrix}`]

	In this situation, the vector is

	[``\begin{bmatrix} x_2-x_1 \\ y_2-y_1 \\ z_2-z_1 \end{bmatrix}
	= \begin{bmatrix} [$a2]-[$a1] \\ [$b2]-[$b1] \\ [$c2] - [$c1] \end{bmatrix}
	= \begin{bmatrix} [@ $a2-$a1 @] \\ [@ $b2-$b1@] \\ [@ $c2-$c1@] \end{bmatrix} ``]

a) To find the line, use the form [`\vec{u} +  t \vec{v}`] where $\vec{u}$ is any point on the line
	(use either of the two points) and the vector between them (found in a).  The result is

	[`` \langle [$a1],[$b1],[$c1] \rangle + t \langle [@ $a2-$a1 @], [@ $b2-$b1@], [@ $c2-$c1@] \rangle``]

END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();    # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
